---
import SEOHead from '../../../components/SEOHead.astro';
import GameNav from '../../../components/GameNav.astro';
import AdSlot from '../../../components/AdSlot.astro';
import SideAd from '../../../components/SideAd.astro';
import InContentAd from '../../../components/InContentAd.astro';
import LevelSelector from '../../../components/LevelSelector.astro';

const title = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 3 Level 4 Walkthrough: Guest Toilet";
const description = "Rooms & Exits Chapter 3 Level 4 walkthrough for Guest Toilet: the eight-digit safe combination 34617058 built from the door plate 346, the Piece of paper marked 17 and the 8 on the toilet roll, plus the picture-frame clue that tells you the combination starts with 3 and ends with 8.";

const faq = [
  {
    q: "What is the safe code in Rooms & Exits Chapter 3 Level 4 Guest Toilet?",
    a: "The wall safe inside the vanity cabinet takes <b>34617058</b> — eight digits, typed in that order on the keypad. We reconstructed it frame by frame from the recording at 30 frames per second: the keys light up one at a time and the eight lit keys are <b>3, 4, 6, 1, 7, 0, 5, 8</b> in that order, with the safe unlocking immediately after the eighth press. It is also consistent with the room's own clue, which says the combination starts with 3 and ends with 8.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where does 346 come from?",
    a: "It is written on the <b>exit door</b> — the white door on the left wall carries <b>346</b> on its upper panel, above and to the left of the handle. It supplies the first three digits of the safe combination. The door itself has no code lock: you open it with the <b>key</b> that comes out of the safe, so 346 is a clue, not something you type at the door.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where does 17 come from?",
    a: "From the <b>Piece of paper</b> in your inventory. It is a hexagonal scrap of paper with a printed pattern and two white characters on it: a <b>1</b> near the top and a <b>7</b> below it. Those are the fourth and fifth digits of the safe combination. We read the item twice, in two separate frames of the inventory screen, and got the same two characters both times.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where does the last 8 come from?",
    a: "The <b>empty cardboard toilet roll</b> on the holder next to the toilet has a single hand-drawn <b>8</b> on it in black. The roll is a clue, not an item you collect: after the paper is removed from the holder the bare core is what you examine. That 8 is the last digit of the combination, and it agrees with the picture-frame clue.",
  },
  {
    q: "What does the picture frame on the shelf tell you?",
    a: "Examining the framed portrait above the toilet triggers a text overlay: <b>THIS CLUE MEAN: THE NUMBER COMBINATION START WITH NUMBER 3 AND END WITH NUMBER 8</b>. That is the game's own wording, grammar included. It tells you the safe's code begins with 3 and ends with 8 — which is exactly how 34617058 is built — but it does not tell you the length, so it is not enough on its own.",
  },
  {
    q: "How many digits does the safe take?",
    a: "Eight. The keypad is a plain 12-key grid — 1 2 3 / 4 5 6 / 7 8 9 / A 0 B — with no display anywhere on the safe, so there is no on-screen counter to tell you how many characters it wants. In the recording eight separate keys are pressed in a row and the door of the safe pops open right after the eighth. If you stop early the safe just sits there, which is why people assume the code is four digits and give up.",
  },
  {
    q: "What are the A and B keys on the keypad for?",
    a: "We could not establish it. The keypad has <b>A</b> at the bottom left and <b>B</b> at the bottom right, with 0 between them, and in the recording neither A nor B is pressed at any point — the eight digits sit between them and the safe opens by itself. They are most likely enter/clear keys, but because we never see them used in this level we do not state that as fact.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where is the safe?",
    a: "Inside the <b>vanity cabinet</b> under the sink, top-left compartment. The cabinet has two doors and four compartments: the safe sits top left, folded grey towels sit bottom left, and the two right-hand compartments are empty. You have to open the cabinet doors before the safe is even visible — it is not on a wall.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is there anything in the toilet bowl or the cistern?",
    a: "No. The recording opens the toilet lid and looks straight down into the bowl and there is nothing inside — no item, no floating clue. The flush plate above the toilet is a dual-flush panel and we never see it used. The only thing on the toilet side of the room that matters is the toilet roll with the 8 on it.",
  },
  {
    q: "What do I do after the safe opens?",
    a: "The <b>Key</b> is already in your bag by <b>0:55</b> — it is picked up while the vanity cabinet is standing open, and the inventory shows it selected with the <i>Key</i> label. Then go to the white door on the left wall, use it there at about 2:07, and the door opens. That is the exit — there is no second code lock anywhere in this room. What the safe itself contained we could not pin down: at 2:03 its door is open, the interior is empty and the sparkles come from inside it, but no item name appears, so we do not claim the key came out of the safe.",
  },
  {
    q: "How long is Guest Toilet, and where does it sit in Chapter 3?",
    a: "Guest Toilet is room <b>4 of 15</b> in Chapter 3, <i>Murder Dressed in White</i>. The recording we worked from runs <b>2:13</b> and finishes on a THANKS FOR WATCHING card at 2:12 without a results panel, so it is one of the shortest rooms in the chapter — a single small bathroom with one safe and one key.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is the door code 346?",
    a: "No. <b>346</b> is painted on the door, but the door has no keypad and no dial — it is a plain lever handle with an escutcheon plate, and the level ends by using the key from the safe on it. 346 is the seed for the safe combination, not a door code. Anyone telling you to type 346 at the door is describing a different level.",
  },
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: f.a.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, "") },
  })),
};
