<body>
  <GameNav />
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &gt; <a href="/rooms-and-exits/">Rooms &amp; Exits</a> &gt; Chapter 3 &gt; Level 4</nav>

  <main class="seo-section">
    <h1>Rooms &amp; Exits Chapter 3 Level 4 Walkthrough: Guest Toilet</h1>

    <p>Guest Toilet is room 4 of Chapter 3, <i>Murder Dressed in White</i>, and it is the smallest room in the chapter so far: one narrow bathroom with a toilet on the back wall, a vanity and mirror on the right, a shelf of ornaments above the toilet, and a door on the left. There is exactly one lock in it — a keypad safe hidden inside the vanity cabinet — plus a key that opens the exit door. This page gives you the safe combination, shows you where every digit of it comes from, and is explicit about the two digits we could not trace to a prop.</p>

    <div class="disclaimer">Unofficial fan-made guide. Not affiliated with Webelinx Games, the developer of Rooms &amp; Exits: Escape Room Games.</div>

    <div class="verify-note">Rebuilt from a single 2:13 recording. The safe combination was read a different way from every other code on this site: the keypad has no display, so we pulled the six seconds of keypad footage at <b>30 frames per second</b> and measured which button changes brightness in each frame. Eight separate presses came out, each localised to one key, in the order <b>3 4 6 1 7 0 5 8</b>, and the safe opens right after the eighth. Every other number on this page (346 on the door, 17 on the paper, 8 on the toilet roll, the clue sentence) was read twice from separate frames, once whole-frame and once from a 2× to 5× crop.</div>

    <LevelSelector chapter={3} current={4} variant="jump" label="Chapter 3 · Murder Dressed in White" />

    <div class="answer-box">
      <span class="label">Quick answer</span>
      <p>Guest Toilet is room 4 of 15 in Chapter 3. One lock, one key: the cabinet safe takes <b>34617058</b>, and the number painted on the door is <b>346</b>.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Open the two doors of the <b>vanity cabinet</b> under the sink. The safe is in the top-left compartment; the towels are below it.</li>
        <li>Read the clues. The <b>exit door</b> carries <b>346</b>. The <b>Piece of paper</b> in your bag carries <b>1</b> and <b>7</b>. The empty <b>toilet roll</b> carries an <b>8</b>. The <b>framed portrait</b> tells you the combination "START WITH NUMBER 3 AND END WITH NUMBER 8".</li>
        <li>Set <b>3 4 6 1 7 0 5 8</b> on the safe keypad, in that order. It is eight digits, not four — the safe opens after the eighth key.</li>
        <li>Find the <b>Key</b> while the vanity cabinet is open (it is in your bag by 0:55) and use it on the white door at about 2:07. That is the exit; the door has no code lock.</li>
        <li>The recording ends at 2:12 on a THANKS FOR WATCHING card, before any results panel — so no reward figure is printed here.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="video-wrap">
      <div class="yt-facade" data-yt="kOUEh4F0Y5A" data-title="Rooms &amp; Exits Level 4 Guest Toilet Walkthrough Murder Dressed in White Chapter 3"
           role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Play video: Rooms &amp; Exits Level 4 Guest Toilet Walkthrough">
        <img src="https://i.ytimg.com/vi/kOUEh4F0Y5A/maxresdefault.jpg"
             alt="Rooms and Exits Chapter 3 Level 4 Guest Toilet walkthrough video" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1280" height="720"
             onerror="this.onerror=null;this.src='https://i.ytimg.com/vi/kOUEh4F0Y5A/hqdefault.jpg'">
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="video-cap">The 2:13 run used for every frame on this page.</p>

    <img class="hero" src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l4-hero-guest-toilet.jpg" alt="Rooms and Exits Chapter 3 Level 4 Guest Toilet: a narrow bathroom with a white toilet against dark grey tiles, a wooden shelf with vases and a framed portrait above it, a white vanity and mirror on the right, and a door on the left" width="1200" height="594" />

    <h2>What this level actually is<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>One bathroom, and it is genuinely small — the whole thing fits in a single camera view. The back wall is split: dark grey tiles at the bottom, warm wood panelling at the top, with a long wooden shelf running between them. On the shelf sit a two-tone vase, a soap dispenser, a bar of soap, the framed portrait, a small round pot and a marble-patterned vase holding a snake plant. Below the shelf is the toilet with a white flush plate above it, a toilet roll holder to its left and a toilet brush to its right. On the right wall: a mirror over a white vanity cabinet with a wooden top and a vessel basin. On the left: the white exit door.</p>
    <p>The floor is the noisiest thing in the room — a grey, white and black patterned tile that looks like it should be a puzzle and is not. We looked at it repeatedly and there is nothing on it; it is decoration.</p>
    <p>Structurally the level is a three-part chain and one lock. Three props hand you digits — the door, the paper, the toilet roll — the portrait tells you how they are ordered at the two ends, and the safe inside the cabinet consumes the result. Then the key from the safe opens the door. That is the whole level, and it took the recording 2:13.</p>

    <h2>The map: what is where<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>Every object we could identify, and what it is for.</p>
    <table class="item-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Object</th><th>Where</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Exit door</td><td>Left wall</td><td>Carries <b>346</b> on the upper panel. Plain lever handle, no keypad. Opened with the key from the safe.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Vanity cabinet</td><td>Right wall, under the basin</td><td>Two doors, four compartments. The safe is top left, folded grey towels bottom left.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Keypad safe</td><td>Top-left compartment of the cabinet</td><td>12-key pad: 1 2 3 / 4 5 6 / 7 8 9 / A 0 B. No display. Code <b>34617058</b>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Framed portrait</td><td>On the shelf, on the wood panelling</td><td>Examining it shows the clue text about the combination starting with 3 and ending with 8.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Toilet roll</td><td>Holder left of the toilet</td><td>Empty cardboard core with a hand-drawn <b>8</b> in black.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Toilet</td><td>Centre of the back wall</td><td>Opens; the bowl is empty. Flush plate above it is never used in the recording.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Mirror</td><td>Above the basin</td><td>Reflects the room; we found no interaction.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Toilet brush</td><td>Right of the toilet</td><td>Scenery — a hotspot in some rooms, but nothing comes of it here.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Piece of paper</td><td>Carried item</td><td>Hexagonal scrap with a pattern and two white characters: <b>1</b> and <b>7</b>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Key</td><td>Cabinet / carried item</td><td>Silver key. In the bag by 0:55 while the cabinet is open; opens the exit door at 2:07.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Powder bottle</td><td>Cabinet / carried item</td><td>Blue bottle that ends up in the bag; we never see it used on anything.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Patterned floor</td><td>Whole room</td><td>Decoration. It looks like a clue and is not one.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Step by step<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>The order below follows the recording. Timestamps are video time; the links jump to the matching second.</p>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 1 · 0:00</span>
      <strong>Sweep the room before touching anything</strong>
      The level opens on the title card and cuts straight into the bathroom. Read it left to right: door on the left wall, toilet and shelf dead ahead, vanity and mirror on the right. There are only five things here that do anything — the door, the cabinet, the framed portrait, the toilet roll and the toilet itself — so the sweep takes ten seconds and saves you opening the same cabinet twice.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l4-hero-guest-toilet.jpg" alt="The Guest Toilet room at the start of Rooms and Exits Chapter 3 Level 4: toilet, shelf, portrait, vanity, mirror and door" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kOUEh4F0Y5A&t=0s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:00</a></div>
    </div>
    <InContentAd />

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 2 · 0:12</span>
      <strong>Open the vanity cabinet — that is where the safe lives</strong>
      The cabinet under the basin has two doors. Open them and the interior splits into four: the <b>safe</b> in the top left, a stack of four folded grey towels in the bottom left, and two empty compartments on the right. The safe is not visible until you do this, which is why people hunt the walls for it. It is a dark grey box with a circular handle on the left and a keypad on the right.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l4-cabinet-towels.jpg" alt="The open vanity cabinet in the Guest Toilet showing folded grey towels and the dark safe in the top-left compartment" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kOUEh4F0Y5A&t=12s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:12</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 3 · 0:18</span>
      <strong>The toilet bowl is empty</strong>
      The lid goes up and the camera looks straight down into the bowl. There is water and nothing else — no item floating in it, no marking on the porcelain. Do not spend time here. The recording does exactly this once and moves on.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l4-toilet-bowl.jpg" alt="Looking down into the open toilet bowl in the Guest Toilet level" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kOUEh4F0Y5A&t=18s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:18</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 4 · 0:32</span>
      <strong>The toilet roll carries an 8</strong>
      The holder beside the toilet has a roll on it. Take the paper and you are left with the bare cardboard core, and the core has a single hand-drawn digit on it in black: <b>8</b>. It is the last digit of the safe combination, and it is the only digit in the room that arrives without any other context — no label, no arrow, just an 8 on a toilet roll.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l4-toilet-roll-eight.jpg" alt="The empty cardboard toilet roll in the Guest Toilet with a hand-drawn 8 on it" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kOUEh4F0Y5A&t=32s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">0:32</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 5 · 1:36</span>
      <strong>The framed portrait gives you the rule</strong>
      Examine the portrait on the shelf and the game puts a text box over the room: <b>THIS CLUE MEAN: THE NUMBER COMBINATION START WITH NUMBER 3 AND END WITH NUMBER 8</b>. That is the wording exactly as it appears, grammar and all. It is the only sentence in the level and it is doing a lot of work: it tells you the combination is ordered, that it opens on 3 and closes on 8, and therefore that 346 (door), 17 (paper) and 8 (roll) are not three separate codes but one sequence.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l4-picture-clue-text.jpg" alt="The clue text over the Guest Toilet room: THIS CLUE MEAN THE NUMBER COMBINATION START WITH NUMBER 3 AND END WITH NUMBER 8" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kOUEh4F0Y5A&t=96s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1:36</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 6 · 1:16 · the door plate</span>
      <strong>346 is painted on the door</strong>
      The white door on the left wall has <b>346</b> on its upper panel, above and to the left of the lever handle. It reads as a room number, and that is almost certainly what it is — but in this level it is also the first three digits of the safe combination, because the clue tells you the combination starts with 3 and 346 is the only 3-leading number in the room. The door itself has no keypad and no dial.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l4-door-number-346.jpg" alt="The white exit door in the Guest Toilet with the number 346 painted on the upper panel" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
      <div class="ts">Watch: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kOUEh4F0Y5A&t=76s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">1:16</a></div>
    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 7 · 1:46 · the paper</span>
      <strong>The Piece of paper carries 1 and 7</strong>
      Open the inventory and select the <b>Piece of paper</b>. It is a hexagonal scrap with a printed grid pattern and two white characters on it: a <b>1</b> towards the top and a <b>7</b> below it. Those are digits four and five of the combination. There is nothing else on the paper — we checked at 4× and the texture behind the two characters is pattern, not small print.
