    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 8 · 1:54 · the keypad</span>
      <strong>Twelve keys, no display, eight digits</strong>
      Zoom in on the safe and the keypad fills the frame: four rows of three, <b>1 2 3 / 4 5 6 / 7 8 9 / A 0 B</b>. There is no screen anywhere on the safe — nothing tells you how many characters it wants, and nothing echoes back what you have typed. The circular handle on the left is the door release, not a dial.
      <img src="/rooms-and-exits/c3l4-safe-keypad.jpg" alt="The keypad on the safe in the Guest Toilet: three columns of 1 to 9 and a bottom row of A, 0, B" width="1200" height="594" loading="lazy" />
