    <h2>What this page could not verify<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <div class="warn">
      Five things, stated plainly so you know which parts of this page are reads and which are reconstruction.
      <br><br>
      <b>1. What the safe contained.</b> At 2:03 the safe is open, its interior is empty and the sparkles come from inside it — the game's "collected" effect — but no item name appears on screen in this run. The <b>Key</b> is already in the bag at 0:55, well before the safe is opened, so we cannot say the key came out of it. What the safe paid out is a genuine gap.
      <br><br>
      <b>2. Where the 0 and the 5 come from.</b> We can see both keys being pressed — 0 at 1:58.3 and 5 at 1:58.7 — and we can see the safe open afterwards, but we could not find a prop in the room that carries either digit. They are not on the door (346), the paper (17) or the roll (8). If a later revision of this page finds their source, the combination stays the same; we are flagging it because it is the one part of the code we cannot derive, only observe.
      <br><br>
      <b>3. What A and B do.</b> The keypad has them and the recording never touches them. Enter and clear are the obvious guesses and we have not printed either as fact.
      <br><br>
      <b>4. The powder bottle and the mirror.</b> A blue bottle ends up in the bag and the mirror is interactive-looking, but we never see either used. They are listed as objects, not steps.
      <br><br>
      <b>5. The reward and the results panel.</b> The recording ends at 2:11 on a THANKS FOR WATCHING card. There is no level-complete card and no coin figure in the footage, so this page prints none.
